            0.132
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Take a square sheet of paper, fold it in the middle and unfold it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.136,
            0.758,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Fold the edges towards the centre line and unfold them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.16,
            0.846,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Fold the top right and bottom left corners onto the creased line to create triangles. Refer to Fig. 5.8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.203,
            0.666,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The triangles should not cross the crease lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.227,
            0.847,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Are a, b and c parallel to p, q and r respectively? Why or why not?"
